Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

AgentSight — https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/agentsight
    RailMon depends on AgentSight twice over, and both are deliberate:

    * as a library — the `agentsight-capture` crate supplies the whole capture
      pipeline: SSL event filtering, HTTP reconstruction, SSE reassembly,
      decompression and credential-header redaction. RailMon composes those
      analyzers rather than reimplementing them.
    * as a binary — the container image downloads the AgentSight release and
      spawns it as the probe.

    The library is a caret requirement in Cargo.toml, its exact version
    recorded in Cargo.lock. The binary is pinned to one release and its
    SHA-256 by the AGENTSIGHT_VERSION and AGENTSIGHT_SHA256 build arguments in
    the Dockerfile. The amd64 image carries the probe; the arm64 image does
    not, because the arm64 image has never been run with upstream's aarch64
    build.

    AgentSight is a project of the eunomia-bpf organisation and is licensed
    under its own terms; see the upstream repository.

Rust crates
    Build and runtime dependencies are declared in Cargo.toml and pinned in
    Cargo.lock, each under its own licence.

